<title>USA: Borders Group authorizes repurchase plan.</title>
<headline>Borders Group authorizes repurchase plan.</headline>
<dateline>ANN ARBOR, Mich. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Borders Group Inc said Tuesday its board authorized and its bank group has provided the necessasry covenant relief to enable a $50 million share repurchase program.</p>
<p>It said the purpose of the program, in part, is to offset future dilution from stock-based incentive plans.  </p>
<p>Neither specific price targets nor timeframes were set for making purchases under the program.</p>
<p>Management said it has no immediate plans to make purchases.</p>
<p>Border's is a retailer of books, music and other educational and entertainment products.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
